    "note": "Round trip out of Boise (Gowen Field), returning to Boise. Filed speed 375 kts, filed altitude 28,000 ft, filed duration 03:53:00, all read directly from Alex's own FlightAware app (screenshot, 2026-08-04 ~12:09 PM MDT, status: Scheduled). Filed route text: ROARR LYONS TWF TCH DTA150030/D1+30 TCH TORIN 4339N/11611W 4345N/11624W 4339N/11611W 4345N/11624W. Plotted below fix-by-fix where a coordinate could be confirmed: ROARR (real FAA fix, 43°17'31\"N/115°22'10\"W, via OpenNav), TWF (Joslin Field/Magic Valley Regional VOR, Twin Falls ID), TCH (WASATCH VORTAC near Salt Lake City, UT, 40.8503N/111.9819W, confirmed via OpenNav), and the DTA150030/D1+30 hold (Delta, UT VORTAC, real coords 39.3806N/112.5077W, hold point computed on the R-150/30nm radial with an approximate +10.5° magnetic-to-true correction for this area -- same method as the FCA/MSO holds on the 8/2 mission, but NOT cross-validated against real ADS-B yet since this flight hasn't departed). LYONS and TORIN omitted -- no reliable public coordinate source found for either, not guessed (same standard applied to VALYY on the 8/2 mission). The trailing '4339N/11611W 4345N/11624W' pair (repeated twice in the filed text) decodes to two points a few miles apart just west of Boise itself; how that fits into the route is not understood and is NOT plotted -- shown honestly as unparsed rather than guessed.",
    "pattern": "Departed KBOI on schedule ~01:00 PM MDT 2026-08-04, live ADS-B track picked up automatically by the pinned-mission poll (no manual tail-tracker entry needed). Confirmed by Alex: mission target is the Widemouth 2 Fire (Millard County, UT, ~2mi SW of Kanosh / near Fillmore -- USFS Fishlake NF, 84,229 ac as of 2026-08-04 18:51 UTC, 0% contained, lightning-caused 2026-07-27, Type 2 incident). Real FDC NOTAM 6/1464 (issued 2026-08-04 0208 UTC) is an active firefighting TFR covering this exact area -- surface to 13,000 ft MSL, active 1200-0400 UTC daily through 2026-08-18, reason 'TO PROVIDE A SAFE ENVIRONMENT FOR FIRE FIGHTING ACFT OPS'. Its boundary is defined by DTA VOR radials (DTA102020.5/DTA119034.3/DTA150044/DTA170040.9/DTA167032.2), which lines up almost exactly with the DTA150030/D1+30 hold in N520NA's own filed route -- the filed hold appears to sit right at/near this TFR's edge, consistent with a research aircraft observing the fire from just outside the restricted block rather than guessing at any special access. Flew a long racetrack/survey pattern almost directly over the fire (repeated passes roughly 38.5-39.2N/112.1-112.6W, the DTA/TCH area) for about 2.5 hours, then transited north back toward Boise, did one wide overflight/reversal pattern northwest of the field (~24nm out) before turning back, descended, and landed at KBOI ~23:23 UTC (~5:23 PM MDT) -- confirmed by two consecutive empty airplanes.live polls right after the last recorded point (43.538N/-116.149W, 3,900 ft, still descending), consistent with the field elevation/coverage gap rather than a real disappearance. **Archived by Alex after landing.** Recorded track below (261 points, downsampled from 3,379) is real ADS-B history pulled server-side from globe.airplanes.live's trace_full endpoint for hex a68a1b, covering the complete flight door-to-door (18:56:56Z departure roll to 23:22:41Z final recorded point) -- this is the actual flown path, not the filed route above. Note: the first archive click only changes in-tab JS state, not this file (same known limitation noted on the 8/2 mission) -- this recorded track was pulled and baked in separately afterward specifically because the live-only version would have been lost on tab close/reload, matching the exact gotcha flagged after the 8/2 mission."
